<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

    <!--
      The grain-backed half of the resource manager's tests: the eleven-step write path and its
      ordering, 404-versus-403, PUT idempotency, operation resumability, cancellation that completes,
      quota lease release, a teardown that fails, and the reconciler conformance suite.

      ⚠ NO Testcontainers AND NO Aspire.Hosting, AND THAT IS A DEVIATION FROM ADR-018 THAT IS OWED
      BACK. docs/plan/02 ADR-018 wants grain behaviour tested "against a real in-process TestCluster
      … with real storage providers backed by Testcontainers", and CyberCloud.Tenancy.Tests does
      exactly that. This project uses Orleans.TestingHost's TestCluster with AddMemoryGrainStorage and
      UseInMemoryReminderService instead, because the environment this was built in could not start a
      container.

      What that costs, stated so it can be paid rather than forgotten:

        - Nothing here proves the state SERIALIZES. In-memory storage keeps the object graph; a real
          provider round-trips it, which is where the "STJ does not populate a get-only collection"
          trap bites. ResourceState and OperationGrainState are the types at risk and every collection
          on both is `{ get; set; }` for that reason — but the assertion that it round-trips is owed.
        - Nothing here proves the DURABLE tier is durable across a silo restart. Resumability is
          tested by deactivating the grain, which exercises the re-drive path but keeps the same
          in-process store.
        - The reminder tests exercise registration and the drive body, not Redis reminder storage
          (docs/plan/04 § Reminders).

      Everything else — ordering, 404-versus-403, idempotency, cancellation, lease release, the
      Deleting-and-visible rule — is behaviour of our code and is fully exercised here.
    -->

    <ItemGroup>
        <PackageReference Include="xunit.v3"/>
        <PackageReference Include="Shouldly"/>
        <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Orleans.TestingHost"/>
        <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Orleans.Reminders"/>
        <PackageReference Include="Orleans.Multitenant"/>
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup Label="Global usings">
        <Using Include="Xunit"/>
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <ProjectReference Include="../CyberCloud.ResourceManager/CyberCloud.ResourceManager.csproj"/>
        <!-- The real quota and index grains — steps 6 and 7 are tested against them, not against fakes. -->
        <ProjectReference Include="../CyberCloud.Tenancy/CyberCloud.Tenancy.csproj"/>
    </ItemGroup>

</Project>
